# Hual02 route (item59, re-authored by item67/item67f/item67g/item85b): player input from the
# vent spawn to Carrington's cell and the exit plateau, objectives driven only by the game's own
# chains, now in the level's own order: eavesdrop (goal 1) -> find the cell (goal 2) -> the cell
# door -> escort (goal 3).
#
# item85b (this tree): the crawl's DetectionVolume21 Touch now fires (the integ-fidelity
# brush-volume PointCheck overlap fix) -> 'demarre_bureau' -> XIIIGoalTrigger3 (91) ->
# Hual02.SetGoalComplete -> SetPrimaryGoal(1): goal 1 "Eavesdrop" promotes during the crawl
# (measured t=20.5). The conversation scene (Cine10 'Standwell' + Cine11 'MacCall', the
# underfloor office at (-760,120)/(-779,-33)) starts at level start (Cine2.CineInit.Begin:
# player controller + CineController.bInitialized + the intro-cartoon wait, CheckpointNumber 1
# -> Play(5)) and sits at tabActions[0] 'wait event demarre_bureau'. The route therefore holds
# in the duct after DV21 and does NOT break the duct's far grate (BreakAbleMover2, Event
# 'grille_brisee') until the conversation completes: breaking it sends Trigger -> Play(2) ->
# the bInterruptive alert Reactions (tabActions3/2 -> turnintosoldier), which interrupt the
# scene and 'blam' never fires (measured both ways, the item85b report). With the wait, Cine11's
# 'event blam' completes goal 1 through XIIIGoalTrigger4 (GoalNumber 1) and fires 'objectif92'
# -> XIIIGoalTrigger6 (92) -> SetPrimaryGoal(2); the scene ends with
# 'playerevent XIIISaveGameTrigger1' (the map's own checkpoint, CheckpointNumber 1 -> 2) and
# both cine pawns 'destroy self' (measured scene end t~62.8 after the t=20.5 DV21 touch; the
# grate shots at t=73/75 keep a ~10 s margin).
#
# Player input (no set_goal/take_control): crouch-crawl through the ceiling vent
# (spawn 104,1840,-4536 -> gallery), one aimed shot breaks the first grate
# (BreakableMover5 at 104,1192 yaw 270, no Event - measured, fires nothing), hold in the duct
# for the conversation (above), two aimed shots break the second grate (BreakAbleMover2 at
# -496,-688 yaw 259.5, Event 'grille_brisee'), crawl the duct and drop into the office floor
# -4856, walk the underfloor to the service lift lobby (the corridor's Porte11 is opened
# by real input: the game's Grab tail -> Porte11.PlayerTrigger), ride the lift (item67:
# the game's own LiftButton0.PlayerTrigger -> LiftManager states -> LiftCage key move;
# the player is carried by the decoded mover-base attachment), then walk out of the floor-2
# cage through the live `LiftDoor1` doorway and follow the map's own surface ReachSpec/PathNode
# chain to the depot reader (item67g). Only the locked `Porte19` gap and the later isolated
# segments are labelled teleports.
#
# item67f: the floor-2 doorway is not `Porte20`. Hual02's `Porte4`/`Porte20` (`XIDCine.Porte`,
# Tags 'porte_bas'/'porte_haut') are serialised `bDeleteMe=true` in a trailing block of 54
# destroyed exports (with the LiftManager's stale XIIIMover0 cage reference); the engine's
# `AActor::IsPendingKill` reports them dead, so they are not part of the live level. No actor in
# the map fires an event named 'porte_haut'/'porte_bas' (the strings occur only as the live
# `LiftDoor` Tags), and the LiftManager's automatic radius search only matches `XIDCine.LiftDoor`.
# The live floor-2 exit is `LiftDoor1`, which the manager's own outer-door states open.
#
# Labelled diagnostic: the hostile BaseSoldier* pawns are removed by the test
# (remove_soldiers; the Cine* scene pawns stay - the conversation needs them). Under the real
# level clock the unmodified level's underfloor gauntlet (BaseSoldier26 (-1714.7,894.9),
# BaseSoldier27 (-2218.2,698.9, shotgun + grenades), BaseSoldier25 (-1923.3,-1094.1), lobby
# BaseSoldier15/28, upper BaseSoldier14) kills the unarmoured player around the underfloor
# walk (measured, the item67 report; crouching does not save the player). That kill is the
# pinned next blocker for playing this level through.
#
# Labelled teleports, each for a measured movement gap (see the report):
# - "depot"          t=422 (-8880,722): after the ride the walker leaves the cage through the
#                    live `LiftDoor1` and follows the map's own nav chain (item67g) across the
#                    surface to the reader (MagneticPassTrigger1 at -5259,803; touched at
#                    t=416.2, used by real input at t=420.5: aim-focus
#                    TargetActor=MagneticPassTrigger1, bCanTrigger=true, Grab runs -> its
#                    PlayerTrigger is the decoded PlaySound-only XIIITriggers.PlayerTrigger).
#                    With no magnetic card, Porte19 (Tag 'Porteentrevs') stays locked, so the
#                    teleport crosses it. The card pickup (Hual02MagneticCardPick4 at
#                    -3474,1550) sits in the petitesalle card room: its entrance Porte21
#                    (Event 'reveil_3') opens by real `use` from the neighbouring zone, but that
#                    zone (the office + card room nav island, 71 PathNodes) is walled off from
#                    the surface corridor except the two `grande_vitre` window panes
#                    (StaticMeshActor8 at -4328,1638 and StaticMeshActor7 at -3354,1632, the
#                    map's only ColCategory-3 blocking meshes; item67j). item84 decoded that
#                    entry closed: ColCategory 3 is `ColType_StaticGlass` (engine.u
#                    Actor.ScriptText enum), but no consumer shatters such an actor - the panes
#                    are script-less Engine.StaticMeshActor exports (0 functions/states),
#                    XIIIBulletsAmmo.ProcessTraceHit's non-pawn branch only runs
#                    Other.TakeDamage (a no-op on them) plus impact FX (GlassImpactEmitter /
#                    BulletScorchGlass / HitMat.HitSound are dressing), and Engine.dll reads
#                    AActor+0x1a0 (ColCategory) nowhere except
#                    execActorInIterationCategory 0x103e6f00 and actor copy/serialize (Xiii.dll
#                    and XIDPawn.dll read it never), so shooting cannot open the island. The
#                    aperture is z -112..16 (sill 112 UU above the walked floors) and no measured
#                    retail primitive crosses it from the flat corridor floor: APawn::physFalling
#                    0x103c37b0 answers a wall hit (normal.Z < 0.7 at 0x10483428) with
#                    processHitWall 0x103bed60 + a TwoWallAdjust slide, never stepUp (walking
#                    only, moveSmooth 0x103b7990 vtbl+0x11c; MAXSTEPHEIGHT 35.0,
#                    Actor.ScriptText) and never a mantle (processHitWall's downward-35 probe at
#                    0x103bef37 runs for AI PHYS_Walking only); jump 92.8 = JumpZ 420 with
#                    PhysicsVolume.Gravity (0,0,-950) < 112 - both pinned by unit tests
#                    (play::sim::tests::*falling*). item85b re-measured the reader-area ladder
#                    shaft (LadderVolume0, live) as a sealed dev leftover: the climb works but
#                    the column is capped at z 1656.8 by the GR_echelles frame's retail
#                    simplified-collision box (12 verts/18 tris), sealed east/west/north at
#                    every probed height, floored at the mouth by the walkable grille1f128
#                    plate, its nav marker Ladder1 is a destroyed export with no ReachSpec, so
#                    the shaft offers no route to the walkway/card room either (report, task 2).
#                    item67j measured the rest of the chain with the card in hand (the committed
#                    probe opt_in_hual02_card_room_reader_chain): the reader use with the card
#                    fires OutEvent 'Porteentrevs' and Porte19 opens, but the corridor west of
#                    Porte19 then pins at x~-6198 against PorteDecors18/19 - decor doors whose
#                    PorteDecors.SetInitialState forces ForeverLocked (its PlayerTrigger only
#                    plays a sound), so the teleport also crosses that seal.
# - "prison entry"   t=428 (-10368,2800): the prison compound perimeter is sealed
#                    in this sim (Porte151 Locked opens only from Carrington's
#                    escort moveseq); the landing touches DetectionVolume14 whose
#                    'didact6' event completes goal 2 through XIIIGoalTrigger1 - now
#                    validating (goal 2 is primary since the conversation's 'objectif92').
# - "prison grille escape" t=434 (-10176,2900): the DV14 landing sits inside the
#                    simplified collision of StaticMeshActor1024 'grille_prison';
#                    measured leg31: the player is pinned until moved.
# - "stair head"     t=482 (-14896,656,438): the exit stairwell pins the walker at
#                    (-14078,1314,35) (measured legs 20-23); the corridor beyond is
#                    sealed by the Locked Porte151, so the exit plateau is entered here.
#
# Weapon grant (labelled diagnostic): the player would carry the Beretta from
# Hual01b (the campaign loadout; Hual01a's route test documents no grant because
# the fresh-login inventory already has it). Starting on Hual02 directly hands the
# Fists only, so the route re-grants xiii.Beretta to make the grate shots real.
#
# Objectives driven by the game's chains on this route (item85b, measured): goal 1 promoted by
# the DV21 crawl touch and completed by the conversation's 'blam'; goal 2 promoted by
# 'objectif92' and completed by the DV14 'didact6' prison landing; goal 3 promoted by
# Porte154 finishing opening (Event 'Carrington_CellDoorOpen' -> XIIIGoalTrigger2 (93) ->
# SetPrimaryGoal(3); NOT by the depot reader - XIIITriggers.PlayerTrigger is decoded
# PlaySound-only) but the escort never starts: TouchTrigger8 sits on a z=63 gallery with no
# navigable access and the corridor's Porte151 opens only from Carrington's escort moveseq,
# which waits forever on the 'soldat_assome' raid event (measured legs 31-37). Goal 0 stays
# promoted-incomplete (the level-end 'fin2' -> XIIIGoalTrigger8 touch fires on the exit plateau
# but the escort goals never complete, so TestGoalComplete never trips), and no travel is
# requested.
t=0.20 crouch 1
t=0.50 goto 104 1840 -4536
t=3.00 goto 104 1730 -4536
t=8.00 goto 104 1400 -4536
t=12.00 yaw 270
t=12.50 grant xiii.Beretta
t=14.00 fire
t=20.00 goto 104 1128 -4536
